# infra/Caddyfile
#
# `admin-dashboard` (C1) task 7.9, design.md D-G. First file in this
# project's history under `infra/` — the directory did not exist before
# this change (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §9/§10 describe it, but no earlier
# change created it). This file is intentionally minimal: only the
# `app.dirus.io` block D-G requires. `api.dirus.io` (machine callers —
# Chatwoot's webhook, A1's `/admin/policies/import`) and `inbox.dirus.io`
# (Chatwoot) are named in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §10's routing table but have
# no corresponding infra config anywhere in this repo yet either — adding
# Caddy blocks for domains with no deployed service behind them yet would
# be inventing infra this phase does not own. Add those blocks in the
# change that actually stands up `api.dirus.io`/`inbox.dirus.io` deployment.
#
# design.md D-G: `handle_path /api/*` on `app.dirus.io` reverse-proxies to
# the API container, stripping the `/api` prefix before forwarding — this
# is why `apps/api/src/app.ts` registers routes with NO `/api` prefix
# (`/auth/me`, `/dashboard/review-queue`, ...) and why
# `apps/dashboard/vite.config.ts`'s dev `server.proxy` strips the same
# prefix, so dev and prod resolve identical backend paths (D-G: "dev/prod
# are structurally identical"). Prod becomes genuinely same-origin this
# way: zero CORS, host-only cookies, no preflight.
#
# `api` here is the API container's service name in
# `infra/docker-compose.prod.yml` (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §10's skeleton);
# port 3000 matches `apps/api`'s own `env.PORT` default and
# `vite.config.ts`'s dev proxy target.

app.dirus.io {
	handle_path /api/* {
		reverse_proxy api:3000
	}

	handle {
		root * /srv/dashboard
		try_files {path} /index.html
		file_server
	}
}
